 "drivingQuestion": "If he covered it properly, how did the animal fall in?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "The mishna is set in a case of internal rot.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_kamma.52a.11",
   "daf": "52a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "כִּסָּהוּ כָּרָאוּי, וְנָפַל לְתוֹכוֹ שׁוֹר אוֹ חֲמוֹר, וָמֵת – פָּטוּר. כֵּיוָן דְּכִסָּהוּ כָּרָאוּי, הֵיכִי נְפַל? אָמַר רַבִּי יִצְחָק בַּר בַּר חָנָה: שֶׁהִתְלִיעַ מִתּוֹכוֹ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If he «covered» the pit «appropriately and an ox or a donkey fell inside and died,» he is «exempt.» The Gemara asks: «Since he covered» the pit «appropriately, how» did it «fall» in? «Rabbi Yitzḥak bar bar Ḥana says:» This is a case «where» the cover «rotted from the inside,» and he could not have known that the cover was damaged. Therefore, he is not responsible for damage caused as a result."
  }
 ],
